WEBVTT

00:13.388 --> 00:15.306
Flowers for you?

00:15.390 --> 00:16.516
Buy some flowers?

00:18.226 --> 00:22.313
-Ugh, why the hell did you drink so much?
-Let go! Get away!

00:24.607 --> 00:26.359
Wow. What a great night.

00:26.443 --> 00:28.695
-Thanks, that was great.
-Thank you, sir!

00:29.195 --> 00:31.990
-Let's go for round three! On me!
-Aah…

00:32.073 --> 00:34.075
-Let's get out of here.
-Round three? No, no.

00:34.159 --> 00:35.660
-I know a great place.
-Listen.

00:35.744 --> 00:37.954
-They do a great pork belly.
-I can't. I gotta go home.

00:38.038 --> 00:39.956
-Take this. You do round three.
-I'm telling you.

00:40.040 --> 00:42.208
-There. Go!
-A round of applause, everyone!

00:43.460 --> 00:45.295
-You don't have to pay. Come on.
-All right…

00:45.378 --> 00:47.338
-Have you researched being a good boss?
-Huh?

00:47.422 --> 00:48.923
-I get it!
-He's already a good boss.

00:49.007 --> 00:50.675
-No need to look that up.
-No, it's nothing.

00:50.759 --> 00:52.927
-How are you getting home?
-I called a driver.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.721
-Let me walk you to your car.
-Get home safe.

00:54.804 --> 00:56.431
-Don't ask what we spend this on!
-Bye!

00:56.514 --> 00:58.516
-Get home safe, sir.
-All right, see you.

01:13.281 --> 01:15.450
Ah. Going to Noeun-dong?

01:19.579 --> 01:21.331
This is my car. Come on, let's go.

01:48.691 --> 01:49.567
Hello?

01:49.651 --> 01:52.153
Hello? You called a driver
for Noeun-dong, right?

01:52.237 --> 01:53.780
-Where are you?
-Driver?

01:53.863 --> 01:56.324
-I'm here, but I don't see anyone.
-I'm already on my way.

01:56.407 --> 01:58.701
Sorry? But I just got here.

01:59.702 --> 02:00.620
What?

02:01.371 --> 02:03.540
Hello? Hello?

02:03.623 --> 02:06.292
Hey, driver.
We're heading to Noeun-dong, right?

02:09.129 --> 02:10.046
Oh…

02:11.005 --> 02:13.424
Ugh. Hey, I think
we're headed the wrong way.

02:14.843 --> 02:17.011
Hey. Excuse me, where are we going?

02:18.972 --> 02:19.931
Driver?

02:29.149 --> 02:31.109
A KILLER PARADOX

02:46.082 --> 02:47.458
Excuse me.

02:47.542 --> 02:49.043
Welcome.

02:49.794 --> 02:51.921
-Hi.
-Hi, uh… how can I help you?

02:52.005 --> 02:54.090
Uh, I was wondering

02:54.174 --> 02:58.052
if you have someone who works here
named Lee Tang.

02:58.136 --> 03:00.013
Oh… Lee Tang?

03:00.513 --> 03:02.891
Uh, it… I mean, the name's unusual.

03:02.974 --> 03:05.351
There's a long A in Tang,
you know, like in Nan.

03:05.435 --> 03:06.477
Oh, yeah, yeah.

03:06.978 --> 03:08.271
He used to work here.

03:09.189 --> 03:10.231
He used to?

03:10.815 --> 03:12.859
Yeah, until a few days ago.

03:14.027 --> 03:15.153
VICTIM'S DETAILS

03:16.196 --> 03:17.238
So

03:18.072 --> 03:21.284
his family repaid
the 950,000 won on his behalf?

03:21.367 --> 03:22.285
Yes.

03:22.952 --> 03:24.078
Well, that's everything.

03:24.162 --> 03:25.830
-Hmm?
-You can go now.

03:25.914 --> 03:26.915
Oh.

03:27.582 --> 03:29.292
-So we're done?
-Yes. All done.

03:29.375 --> 03:31.711
THE PLAINTIFF HAS WITHDRAWN THE COMPLAINT

03:52.523 --> 03:55.318
I'm leaving now.
I wish you all the best.

03:56.319 --> 03:58.780
Hey, Mr. James Park,
come visit sometime.

03:58.863 --> 04:00.615
-I'll buy you a steak.
-Yeah.

04:00.698 --> 04:02.700
All right, get going.

04:03.284 --> 04:06.246
-Have a safe flight.
-All right.

04:06.329 --> 04:07.664
-Goodbye, sir.
-Goodbye, sir!

04:07.747 --> 04:08.831
-Take care!
-Good luck!

04:13.461 --> 04:14.504
Hmm.

04:15.755 --> 04:17.507
The important thing here is that…

04:17.590 --> 04:18.591
Hey.

04:19.634 --> 04:21.135
She's much prettier in person.

04:22.303 --> 04:23.471
Yeah? So what?

04:24.639 --> 04:26.099
How's that gonna help us out?

04:26.599 --> 04:29.435
-It probably won't hurt.
-Whatever. Stop staring at her.

04:31.729 --> 04:32.855
SPECIAL INVESTIGATIONS UNIT

04:32.939 --> 04:36.317
A close examination of the evidence
will tell us what we've missed.

04:36.401 --> 04:38.069
Let's go over it again slowly.

04:38.903 --> 04:41.281
Now we have
a special investigations unit,

04:41.364 --> 04:44.158
it's only a matter of time
before we find the killer.

04:44.242 --> 04:45.702
Or so we thought.

04:46.369 --> 04:48.329
But all we did was waste time.

04:50.290 --> 04:51.165
4 MONTHS LATER

04:51.249 --> 04:53.710
We have nothing to show
for the last four months.

05:00.258 --> 05:02.093
We're back to square one.

05:05.138 --> 05:07.348
I mean, we haven't
solved a single thing yet.

05:07.432 --> 05:09.350
Isn't it too early to demobilize the unit?

05:09.434 --> 05:10.435
Hey.

05:11.144 --> 05:12.562
They won't be here anymore.

05:13.813 --> 05:15.315
They're doing us a favor.

05:17.025 --> 05:20.153
They've been here since before me.
I bet they're itching to go.

05:20.236 --> 05:22.322
NATIONAL FORENSIC SERVICE
CAUSE OF DEATH: UNKNOWN

05:22.405 --> 05:24.032
I've got other cases to work on.

05:24.991 --> 05:26.576
Other cases.

05:26.659 --> 05:28.661
We've still got more than we can handle.

05:29.829 --> 05:32.123
Oh, we miss you, James Park.

05:34.208 --> 05:37.045
Be careful, I don't want
these documents to get out of order.

05:37.670 --> 05:39.714
What did I say?
Pack it so it doesn't fall.

05:39.797 --> 05:41.215
-Huh.
-I don't get it.

05:41.299 --> 05:43.217
They should just hand the case over to us.

05:43.301 --> 05:45.720
What do they expect us to do
after all this time?

05:46.929 --> 05:49.766
Do you think they were really
brought here to bring in bad guys?

05:50.308 --> 05:51.267
Hmm?

05:51.893 --> 05:54.771
Those four months were just to prove
they could keep themselves busy.

05:54.854 --> 05:56.689
It was just a formality, that's all.

05:57.190 --> 06:00.026
-Just a show.
-Right, just a show.

06:00.902 --> 06:03.029
-They just had to show--
-Excuse me.

06:04.697 --> 06:08.368
So all this while, Detective Jang, you
thought we were just putting on a show?

06:12.246 --> 06:15.375
Well, we're leaving anyway,
so I'll just be honest with you.

06:16.000 --> 06:18.920
It's a profiler's job to get
an investigation back on track

06:19.003 --> 06:20.630
when it's falling off the rails.

06:22.423 --> 06:24.842
The cases you showed me
in private aren't serial murders.

06:24.926 --> 06:27.804
You're looking at a bunch
of coincidences, I'm positive.

06:28.304 --> 06:30.181
-If no proof of murder--
-Wait.

06:30.765 --> 06:33.893
So, you've been treating these
as coincidences this whole time?

06:34.769 --> 06:37.647
If there is no proof, we follow
the circumstances before our instincts,

06:37.730 --> 06:38.689
as you know.

06:39.190 --> 06:41.609
Especially in Mr. Kang Sang-muk's case.

06:41.692 --> 06:45.238
His statements about the, uh, date
of the crime, as well as the motive…

06:45.738 --> 06:49.075
-They fit the circumstances at hand.
-And how do they fit, exactly?

06:50.535 --> 06:52.954
You searched the mountains and streams
for four months

06:53.037 --> 06:54.455
but never found that brick.

06:55.456 --> 06:57.959
What suspect forgets
what he did with the murder weapon?

06:58.042 --> 07:01.421
The extreme shock from the situation may
have led him to forget important details--

07:01.504 --> 07:04.966
-Do you really think that makes any sense?
-Tell me why it wouldn't.

07:05.049 --> 07:07.260
We should be open
to all possibilities now.

07:07.343 --> 07:09.470
You've run out of ideas.
You're not being open.

07:09.554 --> 07:11.222
You'll just buy Sang-muk's statement,

07:11.305 --> 07:14.267
and then assume
this is all a coincidence, right?

07:15.435 --> 07:17.395
Detective, I'm gonna say something.

07:17.478 --> 07:20.106
Your team's bias was
clear during the investigation.

07:20.189 --> 07:23.151
-You refused to cooperate--
-So that's the point you wanted to make.

07:24.402 --> 07:27.113
I get that you wanna saddle us
with all the responsibility,

07:27.196 --> 07:28.948
so you can leave here blameless.

07:29.615 --> 07:31.242
Love your show, by the way.

07:31.325 --> 07:33.786
You said this was fun,
and now I saw it firsthand.

07:36.747 --> 07:37.623
Aah.

07:47.175 --> 07:49.302
It airs at ten past ten every Friday.

07:50.219 --> 07:51.762
Make sure you watch it live.

07:51.846 --> 07:53.514
Yeah, I'm a big fan.

07:57.894 --> 07:59.479
Hey, Kim. Hey.

07:59.562 --> 08:00.646
Have you eaten?

08:01.189 --> 08:02.940
-Yes.
-Why'd you eat so early?

08:03.941 --> 08:06.611
Okay. Let's play some badminton, then.

08:07.528 --> 08:08.696
Good for the stomach.

08:10.031 --> 08:11.532
-Now?
-Yes, now.

08:12.200 --> 08:13.993
-Right now?
-Yes. Right now.

08:14.619 --> 08:15.578
Loser buys soju?

08:15.661 --> 08:16.996
-Sure, yeah.
-Hmm.

08:17.497 --> 08:20.291
God. Those dumbasses.

08:20.374 --> 08:22.502
We got some armchair detectives here.
Watch out.

08:24.003 --> 08:28.216
Guys. Don't you think they're relying
too much on behavioral analysis?

08:28.799 --> 08:30.968
They have to approach
it geographically too.

08:31.052 --> 08:34.263
Murderers don't just choose
their crime scenes at random.

08:34.347 --> 08:35.806
They usually stay near their house,

08:35.890 --> 08:38.935
or, at least, they stay
within a pretty small radius

08:39.018 --> 08:41.521
of their normal daily activities.

08:41.604 --> 08:42.647
Come on.

08:43.773 --> 08:45.441
How pathetic.

08:48.110 --> 08:49.111
Aah.

08:49.195 --> 08:50.238
Time to eat.

08:53.491 --> 08:55.535
Yes, jjajangmyeon!

08:56.327 --> 08:57.328
Uh…

08:58.538 --> 09:01.916
-Hello?
-You're lookin' well. You busy?

09:03.209 --> 09:05.127
No, I'm not busy.

09:05.211 --> 09:07.004
But I was just about to eat.

09:07.505 --> 09:08.589
Huh.

09:08.673 --> 09:10.883
So, what brings you here?

09:15.429 --> 09:20.142
So you're saying that these cases look
like a series of serial murders, right?

09:20.226 --> 09:21.936
It's possible, is all I'm saying.

09:22.937 --> 09:24.188
You haven't changed a bit.

09:24.272 --> 09:25.106
QUICK DELIVERY

09:25.856 --> 09:29.944
You're still… how should I put it?
As stubborn and obsessive as I remembered.

09:30.027 --> 09:32.446
Oh, uh, those are kind of expensive.

09:33.030 --> 09:35.032
Please, just be real careful.

09:37.702 --> 09:42.540
Hey, so, don't you think it's
kind of weird that there's no evidence?

09:42.623 --> 09:44.750
-Nothing?
-There's no evidence?

09:44.834 --> 09:47.795
It shows how the police
fumbled the initial investigation.

09:47.878 --> 09:49.797
They can't cooperate or communicate.

09:49.880 --> 09:53.050
To connect the cases,
they need to find at least something, but…

09:53.134 --> 09:55.595
Isn't that how you got caught, hmm?

09:55.678 --> 09:58.347
Oh, come on.
That was a long time ago.

09:58.431 --> 09:59.974
-So?
-That's embarrassing, man.

10:00.558 --> 10:03.311
Cut to the chase.
Is it a serial murderer, or what?

10:05.396 --> 10:06.939
The way I see it,

10:07.023 --> 10:08.441
it's not a serial murderer.

10:08.941 --> 10:10.860
You don't think so? Why not?

10:12.111 --> 10:13.863
-I'm looking at the earlier cases.
-Mm?

10:13.946 --> 10:17.116
The murders don't look premeditated.
They're accidental and impulsive.

10:17.199 --> 10:19.577
The murderer was using blunt weapons
rather than a knife.

10:20.745 --> 10:22.705
But if you look at a later case…

10:22.788 --> 10:24.165
-Here.
-Hmm.

10:24.707 --> 10:26.000
The killer used a knife.

10:27.335 --> 10:29.420
They stabbed the victim four times.

10:29.503 --> 10:31.380
He did that without any hesitation.

10:31.464 --> 10:33.174
As if murder was the sole purpose.

10:33.883 --> 10:34.759
Hmm.

10:34.842 --> 10:38.471
That's what makes this one completely
different from the case you brought me.

10:38.554 --> 10:39.930
-No way it's the same person?
-No.

10:40.014 --> 10:41.891
How would a person go from sharp to blunt?

10:41.974 --> 10:43.309
-Exactly, yeah.
-Hmm.

10:43.392 --> 10:44.477
So I'm thinking,

10:45.436 --> 10:46.646
what if we place

10:47.897 --> 10:49.857
the prosecutor right in the middle?

10:49.940 --> 10:52.360
-Does that make a difference?
-The prosecutor?

10:52.443 --> 10:53.444
Hmm.

10:53.944 --> 10:56.489
That might change the story, then.

10:56.572 --> 10:57.531
-Does it really?
-Yes.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.992
Because Prosecutor Ji
was stabbed with a knife.

11:00.076 --> 11:01.118
-Hmm.
-It was sloppy.

11:01.202 --> 11:02.870
-But the killer stabbed him once.
-Mm-hmm.

11:02.953 --> 11:06.082
So the killer might not have been
as experienced at that point.

11:06.165 --> 11:09.960
But he could've been rehearsing.
And after that, he was doing it perfectly.

11:10.044 --> 11:12.838
-So, could be the killer gradually…
-Evolved from one to another.

11:12.922 --> 11:14.006
-Exactly. Yeah.
-Ah.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.509
So, in fact, a serial murderer is likely.

11:16.592 --> 11:18.010
Yeah, that's right.

11:19.595 --> 11:22.932
-But… don't you find it odd?
-What?

11:23.432 --> 11:26.310
I mean, it's not like the victims
confess their sins to the killer.

11:26.394 --> 11:28.813
So, then, how do they all
end up being criminals?

11:28.896 --> 11:31.691
Isn't that interesting?

11:34.235 --> 11:36.570
So what's Prosecutor Ji's crime?

11:38.781 --> 11:40.616
Awesome, thank you.

11:42.993 --> 11:44.870
Anyway, the conclusion here is that

11:44.954 --> 11:47.498
I don't really think
it's a serial murderer.

11:47.581 --> 11:50.334
-That's just my opinion.
-Mm. Did you hear that?

11:51.585 --> 11:52.712
All right, good.

11:53.254 --> 11:54.630
Okay. I'll let you in.

11:54.714 --> 11:56.382
Wait. Who are you letting in?

11:57.675 --> 12:00.302
You've been hacking
the prosecution's intranet again.

12:00.803 --> 12:03.139
-What?
-Prosecutor Ji's case is confidential.

12:03.222 --> 12:04.890
How'd you know about it in such detail?

12:04.974 --> 12:07.101
Well, it was all over the news.

12:07.184 --> 12:09.687
-Come on in.
-Thanks. Pardon the intrusion.

12:09.770 --> 12:11.731
-Say hi to the detective.
-Who are you?

12:12.648 --> 12:16.110
-Let's go. We'll talk at the station.
-This is an illegal arrest.

12:16.193 --> 12:18.988
You can't do this without a warrant.
This is abuse of power.

12:19.071 --> 12:21.157
-I'm being detained unlawfully. I'm not--
-Here.

12:21.240 --> 12:22.950
Who says we're arresting you?

12:23.033 --> 12:24.618
-You broke his head.
-Hmm?

12:24.702 --> 12:26.787
Choose your fate very carefully, okay?

12:27.329 --> 12:28.164
One.

12:28.873 --> 12:32.960
You can cooperate, come to the station,
answer some questions, and come back home.

12:33.043 --> 12:33.919
Two.

12:34.503 --> 12:37.798
I come back another time
with a search-and-seizure warrant.

12:37.882 --> 12:38.799
Which one?

12:39.967 --> 12:42.553
We might turn this place
upside down while we're at it.

12:43.304 --> 12:46.724
Mr. Profiler, you must love playing
with your toys. Isn't that right?

12:48.601 --> 12:50.728
Bet you'd love putting them back together.

12:56.317 --> 12:58.986
-I can't tell if I can see through this.
-Mr. Roh.

12:59.069 --> 13:01.155
-Yeah?
-Take a seat.

13:02.656 --> 13:03.574
Okay.

13:04.074 --> 13:04.909
What is this?

13:05.785 --> 13:06.702
Why am I here?

13:07.870 --> 13:10.414
You two call the shots,
and you're in the same room.

13:10.498 --> 13:12.625
-Saves me time.
-We're not done yet.

13:13.459 --> 13:16.754
Captain. I admit he looks a little odd.

13:16.837 --> 13:19.507
But if we apply pressure,
we'll find something useful.

13:19.590 --> 13:22.301
You heard him talk
about the prosecutor's case in detail.

13:22.384 --> 13:23.886
I've told you everything.

13:23.969 --> 13:25.971
Know what it feels like at my age

13:26.055 --> 13:29.475
to have the chief scream and spit
in my face 'cause of stunts like this?

13:29.558 --> 13:33.020
-Let me get these in order.
-I'm just trying to retire in peace.

13:34.104 --> 13:36.065
I'm so sick of this nonsense.

13:36.148 --> 13:38.484
Come on, Captain. Please. Huh?

13:44.615 --> 13:47.618
Consider this penance
for the late prosecutor, okay?

13:49.078 --> 13:50.788
We're not sure what it is,

13:50.871 --> 13:53.749
but it's beginning to look
like the man had a lot to hide.

13:54.250 --> 13:57.962
His death is linked to other cases,
so it's the prosecution's headache too.

13:58.045 --> 14:00.005
We're not catching much heat just yet.

14:00.089 --> 14:02.633
But if these turn out to be
serial murders, we'll be in trouble.

14:02.716 --> 14:04.343
-Okay. Okay.
-Give it a try.

14:04.426 --> 14:06.679
If anything comes up,
let me know right away.

14:06.762 --> 14:08.514
-Am I understood?
-Of course, sir.

14:08.597 --> 14:09.682
Hmm.

14:09.765 --> 14:11.517
-Good night, sir!
-All right.

14:11.600 --> 14:14.061
By the books, no mistakes.

14:21.485 --> 14:22.403
-Hey.
-Yeah.

14:22.486 --> 14:24.238
A warrant would just be embarrassing.

14:24.321 --> 14:26.574
Says he found it on some website.
It's a non-starter.

14:26.657 --> 14:27.533
Hmm.

14:27.616 --> 14:30.369
Though there really is
something fishy going on with that guy.

14:30.870 --> 14:33.831
-I mean, I've got nothing at the moment.
-Hmm. Yeah, it's fine.

14:33.914 --> 14:37.084
-Let's send him back for the time being.
-It's okay. Thank you for your help.

14:37.167 --> 14:38.711
-We'll get going.
-Bye.

14:38.794 --> 14:41.338
-Hmm. Wait, wait, wait.
-What?

14:41.922 --> 14:44.049
Did you… want this to happen?

14:44.633 --> 14:48.012
Consider this payback
for that favor I owe you.

14:48.095 --> 14:51.056
This may not be an official investigation,
but the captain gave approval,

14:51.140 --> 14:53.142
so all you need to do is sit tight.

14:53.684 --> 14:54.685
All right?

14:54.768 --> 14:57.187
I'll call later. You did great today, huh?

14:57.271 --> 14:58.981
-Hmm?
-Well, thank you, sir.

14:59.064 --> 15:01.108
-I'm goin' home.
-Good night, sir.

15:02.651 --> 15:04.862
Aren't you hungry?
You didn't eat the jjajangmyeon.

15:07.239 --> 15:09.158
It got all mushy and soggy.

15:09.241 --> 15:11.160
Let's go eat, then. It'll be my treat.

15:12.286 --> 15:13.329
I'm not hungry.

15:14.496 --> 15:17.499
Listen, if you get caught hacking
into the prosecution's intranet again,

15:17.583 --> 15:19.418
I'll really have to have you detained,
huh?

15:19.501 --> 15:21.754
I told you back at my place,
I didn't hack--

15:21.837 --> 15:23.714
Don't jerk me around, you moron.

15:26.383 --> 15:28.302
If you're gonna say something,
just say it.

15:34.683 --> 15:37.895
What do you think the difference is
between coincidence and fate?

15:39.563 --> 15:41.523
Hmm? I mean, think about it.

15:42.983 --> 15:45.402
There are all these murders
happening in Daejeon,

15:45.486 --> 15:47.488
but not a single thing connects them.

15:48.280 --> 15:51.408
I mean, no one can be sure
that there's no connection.

15:52.493 --> 15:54.995
But anyway, that's not on me.
That's your job.

15:55.579 --> 15:57.206
I'm just frustrated, that's all.

15:57.998 --> 15:59.416
We still don't have any leads.

16:02.461 --> 16:04.421
Do you still play superhero these days?

16:05.089 --> 16:08.133
No, I'm not a kid anymore.
I don't do that stuff. No way.

16:09.927 --> 16:12.638
You can do whatever you like,
but you gotta be more careful.

16:12.721 --> 16:14.807
And call me right away
if something comes up.

16:14.890 --> 16:16.892
-For your own good.
-I want to cooperate with you.

16:16.976 --> 16:19.061
I want to catch bad guys too.

16:19.144 --> 16:21.855
You just took things way too far
this time, all right?

16:23.232 --> 16:24.233
I'm serious.

16:26.610 --> 16:28.612
I'm getting something tasty.
Sure you're not eating?

17:30.257 --> 17:31.341
Hmm.

17:32.593 --> 17:33.594
Oh God.

17:52.696 --> 17:54.865
Hey. I wasn't in jail.
What's with the tofu?

17:55.657 --> 17:57.826
I don't know. I saw it on TV.

17:58.786 --> 18:01.789
-We gotta be careful. I'm stressed out.
-Why?

18:02.414 --> 18:04.333
This cop's totally been harassing me.

18:05.250 --> 18:07.669
If you're on his radar,
he's gonna find you. No matter what.

18:09.088 --> 18:10.798
So, then, what do we do?

18:15.761 --> 18:16.887
Excuse me.

18:18.514 --> 18:19.807
I'm with the police.

18:20.849 --> 18:22.184
Let me ask you something.

18:22.267 --> 18:24.686
You frequently deliver to 307, right?

18:26.396 --> 18:28.899
-Hmm.
-Where did you just deliver to?

18:29.399 --> 18:30.442
Unit 307.

18:31.068 --> 18:32.152
Unit 307?

18:34.530 --> 18:36.865
JUNGHWARU
QUICK DELIVERY

18:40.577 --> 18:42.746
Is this guy an accomplice, do you think?

18:42.830 --> 18:44.748
He seemed like a run-of-the-mill nerd.

18:45.290 --> 18:47.793
That's what I thought at first.

18:47.876 --> 18:50.254
But there's more to him
than you'd think.

18:50.337 --> 18:51.964
Meticulous little piece of shit.

18:54.133 --> 18:55.342
What did he do?

18:55.926 --> 18:57.136
A long time ago,

18:58.220 --> 19:00.764
there was this bastard
that I knew I had to catch.

19:01.932 --> 19:04.560
-He was a murderer too.
-Hmm.

19:04.643 --> 19:05.811
And the kid

19:06.311 --> 19:07.688
looked after that murderer.

19:09.982 --> 19:13.652
But I don't know if he's related
to this case or not. I'm just not sure.

19:14.278 --> 19:15.195
But we'll see.

19:17.781 --> 19:19.533
The bastard you just mentioned.

19:20.534 --> 19:21.535
Was it that cop?

19:23.871 --> 19:25.622
Why do you wanna catch this guy so badly?

19:25.706 --> 19:28.208
Christ, we're not on a picnic, man. Huh?

19:29.376 --> 19:30.752
So many questions.

19:35.757 --> 19:37.217
So? Did you ask him?

19:37.968 --> 19:41.305
Yeah. He's from Junghwaru.
An extra large jjajangmyeon to unit 307.

19:41.388 --> 19:44.308
But he's never seen the guy's face well.
He's always wearing his helmet.

19:44.391 --> 19:47.186
-He's always wearing his helmet?
-Yeah, why?

19:48.061 --> 19:49.771
Awesome, thank you!

19:57.529 --> 19:58.822
What? What is it?

19:59.406 --> 20:01.033
-What's going on?
-Get that delivery guy.

20:01.116 --> 20:01.992
-What?
-Sir?

20:02.075 --> 20:04.119
-Now, quickly.
-Sir, wait. What are you doing?

20:27.517 --> 20:28.518
What is it?

20:28.602 --> 20:30.562
What? What's going on?

20:32.105 --> 20:33.232
What's going on?

20:35.817 --> 20:37.569
Hey, what on earth are you doing?

20:38.487 --> 20:40.322
-Hey…
-I knew you'd do this again.

20:42.074 --> 20:44.076
Did you choose the victims for him too?

20:44.159 --> 20:46.411
Choose what victims?

20:48.956 --> 20:51.083
Man, at least just tell me
what's going on.

20:51.166 --> 20:52.793
He can't expect us to chase some guy down.

20:52.876 --> 20:55.087
I didn't see him at first,
but that has to be him, right?

20:55.170 --> 20:56.421
-On the right.
-I think so.

20:56.505 --> 20:58.340
-It is.
-Speed up. Get closer.

21:04.972 --> 21:07.224
-It's the one with "Junghwaru" on it.
-Junghwaru?

21:07.307 --> 21:08.558
Junghwaru, Junghwaru…

21:09.059 --> 21:11.979
All right, so there's two of them.
I can't tell which is which.

21:12.562 --> 21:13.772
-Uh…
-That one. That one.

21:13.855 --> 21:16.108
-Which one?
-License 32561. 3256--

21:16.191 --> 21:18.610
That one? Way up front? Are you sure?

21:18.694 --> 21:19.528
Yeah.

21:19.611 --> 21:20.737
I'll go catch him.

21:24.324 --> 21:25.325
Scuse me!

21:26.868 --> 21:27.786
Scuse me!

21:31.248 --> 21:33.292
Hold on! Junghwaru!

21:34.084 --> 21:34.960
Hey!

22:09.953 --> 22:12.539
Here we go. One, two, three.

22:13.832 --> 22:15.417
Wait, no. This is crazy heavy.

22:22.799 --> 22:24.926
Hey, Junghwaru.

22:27.596 --> 22:29.056
Call Lee Tang right now.

22:30.849 --> 22:32.893
Who's Lee Tang? I don't know him.

22:33.810 --> 22:36.438
-Oh, you don't know who he is? Huh?
-That's right.

22:36.521 --> 22:37.773
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

22:37.856 --> 22:40.233
Don't fucking play dumb,
you stupid little shit.

22:41.360 --> 22:43.362
Now tell me how you hid the evidence.

22:43.445 --> 22:44.571
Hid the evidence?

22:44.654 --> 22:47.366
-Do you have proof that I--
-Answer me, asshole.

22:47.908 --> 22:50.994
This is what you do, pick targets
based on a guess, with no evidence.

22:51.078 --> 22:53.288
You miss the culprit every time.
That's why I--

22:54.373 --> 22:57.584
-This is how you missed the guy last time!
-What did you just say, asshole?

22:57.667 --> 23:00.253
-Who did I miss?
-Excessive force! Excessive force!

23:00.337 --> 23:01.755
Excessive force?

23:01.838 --> 23:03.215
How is this excessive, huh?

23:04.007 --> 23:06.927
Hey, is it excessive force
when you're resisting arrest?

23:07.761 --> 23:09.054
Is it?

23:09.930 --> 23:13.850
Answer me, smart-ass. You use fancy words
and think you can get away with this?

23:13.934 --> 23:15.769
Huh? Hey.

23:15.852 --> 23:17.729
Spill it, you son of a bitch.

23:17.813 --> 23:19.564
Sir.

23:19.648 --> 23:21.108
-I caught him.
-Bring him here.

23:21.191 --> 23:22.859
-I can't be here right now.
-Hold on.

23:22.943 --> 23:24.361
-My boss'll be pissed.
-Who's this?

23:24.444 --> 23:26.238
The Junghwaru delivery guy.

23:26.321 --> 23:28.865
-This isn't the guy I told you to catch!
-Yong-jae.

23:28.949 --> 23:30.409
-I didn't do anything!
-He's not?

23:30.492 --> 23:31.827
-God, this sucks.
-Who is this guy?

23:31.910 --> 23:34.329
-Yes, sir.
-Is Nan-gam with you? Put him on.

23:34.413 --> 23:36.331
-The captain wants to talk to you.
-Look--

23:36.415 --> 23:38.583
-Okay, so am I free to go?
-Hold on, hold on.

23:38.667 --> 23:40.252
-Moron.
-Jang Nan-gam!

23:41.128 --> 23:42.504
-Yes, sir.
-Oh, there he is.

23:42.587 --> 23:45.048
-Why haven't you answered my calls?
-I'm a little busy.

23:45.132 --> 23:47.300
-Can I call you later?
-No. This can't wait.

23:47.384 --> 23:49.553
It's all over the internet, you damn punk!

23:49.636 --> 23:52.973
-What are you doing at Roh Bin's place?
-What's all over the internet?

23:53.056 --> 23:54.516
Video of you beating him.

23:54.599 --> 23:56.309
-It's everywhere, you idiot!
-Huh?

23:56.810 --> 23:59.729
-You can't barge in and rough him up!
-Open up!

23:59.813 --> 24:02.524
-We're getting calls about a cop--
-I'll call you back.

24:03.108 --> 24:04.568
You hear that, too, right?

24:05.569 --> 24:06.987
I think they're in there.

24:08.947 --> 24:10.532
We're here about the report!

24:11.700 --> 24:14.578
I'll try and get them to open up.
You call the office.

24:14.661 --> 24:16.621
This is the police.

24:17.747 --> 24:19.833
Open the door.

24:21.042 --> 24:23.503
If you don't,
we will open it by force.

24:29.384 --> 24:31.428
Open up right now!

24:33.054 --> 24:35.432
Open this door now!

25:56.263 --> 25:59.391
4 MONTHS AGO

26:08.358 --> 26:09.568
"Dear Mom and Dad,

26:11.695 --> 26:13.321
I was born into this world,

26:14.072 --> 26:17.617
but I couldn't figure out
what purpose I could serve while I'm here,

26:17.701 --> 26:19.828
so I've just been an aimless loser."

26:24.040 --> 26:25.834
"But I'm going on a journey…

26:27.794 --> 26:29.713
to find a way to right my wrongs."

26:31.381 --> 26:32.340
"I'm

26:33.341 --> 26:34.551
going to Canada."

26:38.805 --> 26:39.764
"Please forgive me

26:41.141 --> 26:42.475
for not saying goodbye."

26:52.694 --> 26:54.529
BALANCE: 358,000 WON

26:54.613 --> 26:56.406
It's been revealed
that Lee and Kang,

26:56.489 --> 26:59.618
high-school students who were murdered
in Dunsan-dong on the 3rd,

26:59.701 --> 27:03.788
turned out to be perpetrators of violence
in their school, shocking the public.

27:03.872 --> 27:05.707
They sexually assaulted a girl
in middle school…

27:05.790 --> 27:08.376
"I just don't think
I can bring myself to stay

27:08.460 --> 27:10.462
and pretend that everything's normal."

27:11.004 --> 27:11.963
"That's why."

27:12.047 --> 27:13.381
What are you doing?

27:14.174 --> 27:17.052
"I know
that I'll make new friends there."

27:17.886 --> 27:18.970
"I'll work hard."

27:20.347 --> 27:21.723
"And then I'll come back

27:22.641 --> 27:25.310
as a better person, as someone decent."

27:33.526 --> 27:34.819
"Don't worry about me."

27:38.865 --> 27:41.242
NO SEARCH RESULTS FOR "ONLYFORHEROES"

27:48.958 --> 27:52.671
TODAY, WE'LL LEARN ABOUT WHAT HAPPENS IF
YOU DON'T APPEAR FOR AN ATTENDANCE REQUEST

27:52.754 --> 27:55.423
THE COMPUTER WILL SHUT OFF SOON

27:56.925 --> 27:58.885
"I'll start over from scratch."

28:51.271 --> 28:53.648
There are no more trains
in service today.

28:54.274 --> 28:57.026
Any passengers
on the platform or in the waiting area,

28:57.110 --> 29:00.238
please exit the station
and use another transit service.

29:01.406 --> 29:04.284
-Thank you for your understanding.
-Um, I'm Onlyforheroes.

29:06.286 --> 29:07.829
I'm sorry for the wait.

29:07.912 --> 29:11.458
I'm from Daejeon. And I really think
that I can help you out, Mr. Tang.

29:11.541 --> 29:13.001
I promise I'm not a weirdo.

29:13.084 --> 29:17.088
-I came all this way because I wanna help.
-This is the final stop. Please get off.

29:18.423 --> 29:20.759
Please step out.
This train is not in service.

29:20.842 --> 29:22.343
REMAINING DISTANCE: 120 KM

29:26.556 --> 29:29.476
This is an accident-prone area.

29:29.559 --> 29:30.894
Please be careful.

29:31.853 --> 29:34.564
I've been searching for you
for a long time, Mr. Lee.

29:35.482 --> 29:37.609
You see, there's this thing called "fate."

29:40.111 --> 29:42.280
Some people are
meant to cross paths.

29:45.283 --> 29:48.161
You know,
I think we were destined to meet.

29:51.164 --> 29:53.792
If we were to work together,

29:54.501 --> 29:55.835
we could change the world.

29:56.377 --> 29:57.837
What is it that you do?

29:57.921 --> 30:00.298
-I'm a sidekick.
-What?

30:01.132 --> 30:05.053
Batman and Robin.
Sherlock and Watson. Goku and Krillin.

30:05.595 --> 30:07.222
Lee Tang and Roh Bin.

30:09.432 --> 30:12.352
That's my name.
I even had it legally changed.

30:20.819 --> 30:21.778
Huh.

30:22.529 --> 30:23.905
Is this some kinda sick joke?

30:23.988 --> 30:25.990
Yeo Bu-il, Seon Yeo-ok,

30:26.074 --> 30:28.785
and, uh, Kang Jae-jun and Lee Jin-seong.

30:28.868 --> 30:30.245
I believe you've met them.

30:30.328 --> 30:32.121
Uh, how did you get this?

30:32.205 --> 30:35.333
I told you.
I've been hard at work looking for you.

30:38.044 --> 30:42.549
I was baffled too. Someone I was looking
for suddenly appearing before my eyes?

30:45.009 --> 30:48.221
But I had to make extra sure.
It took me a while.

30:48.304 --> 30:50.723
TOMORROW, 12. HOUSE WITH BLUE DOORS
BY THE YONGUN INTERSECTION

30:51.307 --> 30:54.853
You only suspected you have special
powers, but you were never fully sure?

30:56.145 --> 30:57.272
Take a look at this.

31:00.191 --> 31:02.402
What do you think
these cases have in common?

31:06.322 --> 31:08.575
One, all the victims were pieces of shit.

31:08.658 --> 31:12.871
Two, you didn't get rid of any evidence
after, but it did just disappear, right?

31:14.539 --> 31:15.999
The evidence…

31:16.082 --> 31:17.584
What could all of this mean?

31:19.586 --> 31:23.590
The way I see it, some higher power
is telling you to continue your work.

31:24.173 --> 31:27.510
For me, that's the only explanation.

31:29.095 --> 31:31.389
It's unreal. Doesn't make sense.

31:32.432 --> 31:33.683
What do you want from me?

31:35.935 --> 31:37.520
To serve justice with you.

31:38.980 --> 31:41.107
-Huh?
-Let's work together, Mr. Lee.

31:42.483 --> 31:44.360
I'll give you anything that you want.

31:45.445 --> 31:48.781
I have 50 million won.
It's my life savings.

31:48.865 --> 31:51.159
If you need any money,
I'll give it to you.

31:51.242 --> 31:54.871
And you said you wanted to visit
the Rocky Mountains someday, didn't you?

31:54.954 --> 31:56.623
I can send you there if you want.

31:56.706 --> 31:59.584
So I'm asking you,
please, can we just give it a try?

32:00.251 --> 32:01.586
I… I'm serious.

32:07.884 --> 32:09.761
No, no…

32:09.844 --> 32:10.845
Uh, I…

32:10.929 --> 32:12.513
You did nothing wrong, Mr. Lee.

32:12.597 --> 32:14.849
All you did was clean up human garbage.

32:15.642 --> 32:18.645
Cleaning up isn't a crime,
so there's no need for you to run.

32:18.728 --> 32:20.521
That's all I'm trying to tell you.

32:20.605 --> 32:22.482
If you decide to work with me,

32:23.149 --> 32:25.568
I'll make it
so you don't have to run anymore.

33:08.653 --> 33:09.821
Want some breakfast?

33:11.572 --> 33:13.700
So, in simple terms,

33:14.367 --> 33:16.077
your powers work like this, okay?

33:16.577 --> 33:18.079
When you see a piece of trash,

33:18.579 --> 33:19.914
you want to throw it away.

33:20.415 --> 33:25.044
And of course, what you do is
you trash the trash, obviously.

33:26.587 --> 33:28.923
Hey!
That man over there just littered!

33:29.007 --> 33:30.091
Wait, hold on.

33:31.509 --> 33:34.220
So, what? I just start
stabbing people on the subway?

33:34.303 --> 33:36.264
And you're saying
they'll all have deserved to die?

33:36.347 --> 33:39.684
And that the evidence will disappear?
That makes no sense.

33:42.478 --> 33:43.479
Look, have you ever

33:44.480 --> 33:45.356
felt an urge?

33:45.440 --> 33:48.276
I mean, have you gotten a sign to do it?

33:50.570 --> 33:51.404
No.

33:52.280 --> 33:53.156
That's perfect.

33:53.740 --> 33:55.533
That's also part of your powers, then.

34:00.163 --> 34:03.082
In order to throw away trash,
you need to have a trash can.

34:04.792 --> 34:07.879
Bearing all that in mind,
I think we were destined to meet.

34:08.755 --> 34:11.215
Of course, the decision is up to you.

34:14.469 --> 34:15.553
Hey.

34:16.763 --> 34:17.680
Sleep over.

34:21.142 --> 34:23.269
-By the way, hyung.
-Yeah?

34:25.480 --> 34:28.191
You said you had two partners before me.

34:28.816 --> 34:30.109
Where are they right now?

34:30.985 --> 34:31.986
You've already seen

34:33.029 --> 34:34.655
one of them already.

34:36.741 --> 34:38.201
And the one before him…

34:40.244 --> 34:42.038
I hope we never have to see him again.

34:43.956 --> 34:45.208
Who… who is that?

34:48.336 --> 34:51.506
There's some stuff
behind the shelf.

34:53.925 --> 34:55.927
Take what you want from there.

35:00.556 --> 35:03.351
PERSONAL DETAILS
YEO BU-IL

37:15.775 --> 37:16.817
I'm sorry.

37:17.818 --> 37:18.694
Are you okay, sir?

37:18.778 --> 37:20.029
Ah, it was nothing.

37:20.112 --> 37:22.073
He should apologize
for bumping into you.

37:22.156 --> 37:23.532
Nah, it's fine…

37:24.325 --> 37:26.577
For a prosecutor,
you're very forgiving.

37:36.045 --> 37:38.547
Ah. Going to Noeun-dong?

37:39.131 --> 37:40.925
This is my car. Come on. Let's go.

38:34.061 --> 38:35.688
All I've ever done is work.

38:36.188 --> 38:37.773
It's not a crime, please.

38:37.857 --> 38:39.191
I have a family.

38:39.275 --> 38:41.402
My daughter, she started middle school.

38:41.986 --> 38:44.280
What else was I supposed to do? Huh?

38:44.780 --> 38:47.241
Look, please,
just tell me what I did wrong.

38:47.325 --> 38:49.452
Say it. Tell me what I did.

38:49.535 --> 38:51.787
-Please.
-Yeah, I know.

38:53.497 --> 38:56.250
-Why do I even want to kill you?
-Wait.

38:58.419 --> 39:00.796
Wait. What do you mean?

39:02.340 --> 39:04.216
What crime could you have done?

39:04.967 --> 39:07.511
-What?
-To have brought us both here tonight?

39:07.595 --> 39:10.139
How am I even supposed to know?

39:12.558 --> 39:16.312
You don't know a single thing
about my life.

39:26.322 --> 39:27.948
I think he might tell us.

39:28.032 --> 39:28.949
What?

39:33.704 --> 39:35.081
Okay.

39:35.581 --> 39:40.002
This is why
I can't ever save up any money.

39:43.255 --> 39:44.256
Okay.

39:45.091 --> 39:45.966
We're in.

39:46.967 --> 39:47.927
Hmm…

39:53.265 --> 39:54.141
Hey.

39:54.642 --> 39:55.518
Hey!

39:59.397 --> 40:02.024
-Hey, you've got curly hair.
-Uh, sir! Excuse me!

40:02.108 --> 40:04.360
Please! I can explain!

40:04.443 --> 40:05.694
-Okay?
-Hey.

40:05.778 --> 40:08.406
-You're too pretty to be crying like this.
-I can explain!

40:08.489 --> 40:10.699
-Let's talk about this rationally!
-Stop struggling.

40:10.783 --> 40:11.992
Okay? Sir!

40:12.076 --> 40:13.786
-Good job.
-Please, sir!

40:13.869 --> 40:15.579
-Stay still. Shut up.
-I can explain!

40:15.663 --> 40:18.290
-Stop crying, you bitch!
-Fuck! Hey. Sir! Sir!

40:18.374 --> 40:20.292
It… it's not what it looks like!

40:20.376 --> 40:23.003
You… you're doing this for money,
aren't you?

40:23.087 --> 40:26.507
I can give you money!
I will! Okay? I will pay you.

40:26.590 --> 40:28.676
I will. Wait. Wait, wait!

40:28.759 --> 40:30.010
I'm sorry!

40:30.094 --> 40:31.887
I'm so sorry! I'm sorry!

41:20.895 --> 41:22.021
Why don't we go home?

41:25.232 --> 41:26.066
Home?

41:29.320 --> 41:31.780
Look, Roh Bin, I wanna live on my own.

41:49.965 --> 41:52.259
One, two. Good.

41:52.343 --> 41:54.512
Ah, you're back again? Ready to work out?

41:54.595 --> 41:55.471
Good, great!

41:55.554 --> 41:56.889
Really lean into it, okay?

41:56.972 --> 42:00.017
All right! One, two! There you go!

42:13.489 --> 42:17.576
HOW IS THIS UNJUSTIFIED
WHEN YOU'RE RESISTING ARREST?

42:20.746 --> 42:22.039
God damn.

45:09.456 --> 45:10.708
Hey, I'm back.

45:13.961 --> 45:15.045
Scuse me.

45:16.588 --> 45:18.757
Boss, are we behind on deliveries?

45:19.967 --> 45:21.885
Shit. I said we need more guys.

45:26.223 --> 45:27.474
Can I ask you somethin'?

45:28.142 --> 45:29.059
Me?

45:36.275 --> 45:37.276
Yeah.

45:37.359 --> 45:39.653
SONG CHON
NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

45:44.283 --> 45:46.452
You know this man, that right?

45:47.411 --> 45:48.537
Oh, yeah.

45:48.620 --> 45:49.955
It's Tang, sure.

45:50.581 --> 45:51.623
Huh.

45:51.707 --> 45:52.875
-Why--
-Where'd he go?

45:55.711 --> 45:56.670
It's all right.

45:57.671 --> 45:59.089
Just wanna talk to him.
